**Before/after:**
```ts
// Before
const data = await pendingTasks.run(async () => fetchData());

// After
pendingTasks.run(async () => { await fetchData(); });
```
`PendingTasks.run` now returns `void`, so its resolved value can no longer be used.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// Before
const data = await pendingTasks.run(async () => fetchData());

// After
const removeTask = pendingTasks.add();
try { const data = await fetchData(); /* use data */ }
catch (e) { /* handle rejection explicitly */ }
finally { removeTask(); }
```
Rejections must be handled manually when using `PendingTasks.add`, since unhandled rejections can shut down the Node process under SSR.

