**Before/after:**
```ts
// before — assumes a synchronous result
const target: string | UrlTree = redirectFn(data);

// after — return type is now MaybeAsync<string | UrlTree>
const result = redirectFn(data); // string | UrlTree | Observable<string | UrlTree> | Promise<string | UrlTree>
const target: string | UrlTree = isObservable(result)
  ? await firstValueFrom(result)
  : await result;
```

Run a build or type-check and look for errors where an explicitly typed writable array parameter is forwarded to a Router method whose parameter is now readonly.

**Before/after:**
```typescript
// v19.2.0
createUrlTree(commands: any[], navigationExtras: UrlCreationOptions = {}): UrlTree;

// v20.0.0
createUrlTree(commands: readonly any[], navigationExtras: UrlCreationOptions = {}): UrlTree;
```

Where a parameter is declared as a writable array (for example `commands: any[]` or `string[]`) and forwarded to the Router method, widen the declaration to the matching readonly array type.

**Before/after:**
```typescript
// before
function go(commands: any[]) { return router.createUrlTree(commands); }

// after
function go(commands: readonly any[]) { return router.createUrlTree(commands); }
```

Re-verify the values in the `Route` guard arrays so each entry is a functional guard (`CanActivateFn`, `CanMatchFn`, `CanActivateChildFn`, `CanDeactivateFn`, `CanLoadFn`) or a DI token matching `ProviderToken<T>|string`.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// before: accepted any (unchecked)
{ path: 'a', canActivate: [someValue] }

// after: must be a functional guard or DI token
{ path: 'a', canActivate: [myGuard] }            // CanActivateFn
{ path: 'a', canActivate: [MyGuardToken] }       // ProviderToken<T> | string
```

